{
    "map": {
        "description": "Makes a feature layer from a netCDF file.",
        "dimension_values.descr": "<xdoc><p>The value (such as 01/30/05) of the dimension (such as time) or dimensions to use when displaying the variable in the output layer. By default, the first value of the dimension or dimensions will be used.</p><ul><li>Dimension—A netCDF dimension.</li><li>Value—The dimension value to use.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "dimension_values.dt.title1": "Dimension",
        "dimension_values.dt.title2": "Value",
        "dimension_values.title": "Dimension Values",
        "in_netcdf_file.descr": "The input netCDF file.",
        "in_netcdf_file.title": "Input netCDF File",
        "m_variable.descr": "A netCDF variable used to specify linear measurement values (m-values) for features.",
        "m_variable.title": "M Variable",
        "out_feature_layer.descr": "The name of the output feature layer.",
        "out_feature_layer.title": "Output Feature Layer",
        "row_dimension.descr": "<xdoc><p>The netCDF dimension, or dimensions, used to create features with unique values in the feature layer. The dimension or dimensions set here determine the number of features in the feature layer and the fields that will be presented in the feature layer&apos;s attribute table.</p><p>For instance, if StationID is a dimension in the netCDF file and has 10 values, by setting StationID as the dimension to use, 10 features will be created (10 rows will be created in the feature layer&apos;s attribute table). If StationID and time are used, and there are 3 time slices, 30 features will be created (30 rows will be created in the feature layer&apos;s attribute table). If you will be animating the netCDF feature layer, it is recommended, for efficiency reasons, to not set time as a row dimension. Time will still be available as a dimension that you can set to animate through, but the attribute table will not store this information.</p></xdoc>",
        "row_dimension.title": "Row Dimensions",
        "title": "Make NetCDF Feature Layer",
        "value_selection_method.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the dimension value selection method that will be used.</p><ul><li><span title=\"BY_VALUE\">By value</span>—The input value will be matched with the actual dimension value.</li><li><span title=\"BY_INDEX\">By index</span>—The input value will be matched with the position or index of a dimension value. The index is 0 based; that is, the position starts at 0.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "value_selection_method.domain.BY_INDEX": "By index",
        "value_selection_method.domain.BY_VALUE": "By value",
        "value_selection_method.title": "Value Selection Method",
        "variable.descr": "The netCDF variable, or variables, that will be added as fields in the feature attribute table.",
        "variable.title": "Variables",
        "x_variable.descr": "A netCDF coordinate variable used to define the x, or longitude, coordinates of the output layer.",
        "x_variable.title": "X Variable",
        "y_variable.descr": "A netCDF coordinate variable used to define the y, or latitude, coordinates of the output layer.",
        "y_variable.title": "Y Variable",
        "z_variable.descr": "A netCDF variable used to specify elevation values (z-values) for features.",
        "z_variable.title": "Z Variable"
    }
}
